## Bottom line

The paper is **scientifically tractable to replicate fully** because the authors did publish the
complete equation set and parameter values, but it is **practically friction-heavy** because the
empirical foci-count data and the simulation source code are both withheld. A campaign-style
short-form first pass can confidently confirm only the two closed-form quantities reproduced
here. A full replication of Figs. 5–7 is a **tier-2** task estimated at 2–4 person-days; it is
appropriate to schedule against any pipeline implementing a generic mass-action DSB-repair model
(e.g. as a comparator for MEDRAS-MC or NASIC-DNA in the LUCID100 portfolio).


